  "final_answer_text": "Good news: the Otter preset (`vehicle-a-otter`, planar3 plant, validated) is available. Before I add sensors, two things need decisions:\n\n**1. Sensor choice — position tracking has more than one plausible candidate:**\n\n| Plugin | Domain | What it gives you |\n|---|---|---|\n| `gps` | ABSOLUTE_POSITIONING | Direct absolute position fixes (lat/lon or NED) |\n| `imu` | RELATIVE_POSITIONING | Accelerations/angular rates — supports dead-reckoning, not standalone position |\n| `ins-gps-fusion` | DERIVED | Fused position/attitude estimate combining GPS+INS (needs GPS+IMU present to be meaningful) |\n\n- If you just want ground-truth-ish absolute position logging → **`gps`** alone.\n- If you want a fused, more realistic navigation-grade position estimate (accounting for IMU drift/GPS updates) → **`gps` + `imu` + `ins-gps-fusion`**.\n\n**My default (if you don't specify):** add `gps` alone, since it's the simplest sensor that directly satisfies \"position tracking.\" Let me know if you'd prefer the fused GPS+IMU+INS stack instead.\n\n**2. I don't yet have a scenario to attach sensors to.** To construct/validate the Otter scenario I need the required fields:\n- `experiment`: name, seed, timestep_s, duration_s\n- `backend`: type (browser/node/tensor-cpu/tensor-mps/tensor-cuda)\n- `mission`: waypoint list (or surveyor-waypoint w/ origin+erp)\n\nCould you provide these, or should I use reasonable defaults (e.g., `node` backend, 0.1s timestep, 60s duration, seed 0, a simple 2-waypoint straight-line mission)? Please confirm defaults or give specifics, and confirm the sensor choice, and I'll build and validate the scenario.",
